  "summary": "Teamwork develops patience, empathy, confidence, negotiation, communication, and self-awareness. Working with people who think differently reveals personal blind spots. Collaboration also teaches indi",
  "explanation": "### Personal benefits\nTeamwork develops patience, empathy, confidence, negotiation, communication, and self-awareness. Working with people who think differently reveals personal blind spots. Collaboration also teaches individuals to accept feedback and to separate the quality of an idea from their personal identity.\n\n### Professional benefits\nOrganizations rely on teams to deliver complex outcomes. Effective collaboration reduces duplicated work, improves quality, strengthens innovation, and makes problem-solving faster. Team-oriented professionals are better prepared for cross-functional projects and leadership responsibilities.\n\n### Long-term impact\nA reputation for reliability and generosity creates stronger professional relationships. People who share credit, document knowledge, and help others develop are often trusted with important work. Poor collaboration has the opposite effect: missed commitments and defensive behavior reduce trust over time.\n\n### Case illustration\nA student project team repeatedly missed milestones because tasks were assigned verbally and no one knew which work depended on another. The team introduced a shared task board, weekly planning, and a five-minute review of blockers. Progress improved because the system clarified ownership and dependencies rather than simply demanding more effort.",
