  "summary": "Rate from 1 (rarely) to 5 (consistently): I understand shared goals; I meet commitments; I communicate risks early; I listen fairly; I invite other views; I document decisions; I give useful feedback;",
  "explanation": "### Rating questions\nRate from 1 (rarely) to 5 (consistently): I understand shared goals; I meet commitments; I communicate risks early; I listen fairly; I invite other views; I document decisions; I give useful feedback; I handle disagreement respectfully; I ask for help; I share knowledge; I support quieter members; I reflect after projects.\n\n### Scoring guide\n48-60 indicates a strong foundation; 36-47 indicates developing competence; 24-35 suggests focused practice is needed; below 24 suggests beginning with basic reliability, listening, and role clarity. The score is a reflection aid, not a formal diagnosis.\n\n### Prompts\nWhen have I contributed most effectively? When did I withdraw or dominate? What team behavior frustrates me, and how might I respond constructively? Which commitment do I need to manage better? What one action will make collaboration easier for my team this week?",
