  "explanation": "### Books\n1. The Five Dysfunctions of a Team by Patrick Lencioni--team health and trust. 2. Team of Teams by Stanley McChrystal--adaptability and shared consciousness. 3. Crucial Conversations--high-stakes dialogue. 4. Drive by Daniel Pink--motivation and autonomy. 5. Multipliers by Liz Wiseman--developing others.\n\n### Online resources\nCoursera (https://www.coursera.org), edX (https://www.edx.org), Atlassian Team Playbook (https://www.atlassian.com/team-playbook), and Toastmasters (https://www.toastmasters.org) provide learning materials and practice opportunities.\n\n### Practice sources\nUse peer-learning circles, student organizations, volunteer projects, retrospectives, and workplace mentoring. Prioritize resources that include exercises, feedback, and real collaboration rather than passive reading alone.",
