  "summary": "Leadership practice develops confidence, judgment, communication, empathy, and initiative. It teaches individuals to take responsibility rather than waiting for perfect instructions.",
  "explanation": "### Personal benefits\nLeadership practice develops confidence, judgment, communication, empathy, and initiative. It teaches individuals to take responsibility rather than waiting for perfect instructions.\n\n### Professional benefits\nOrganizations benefit from leaders who align work, remove obstacles, make decisions, and develop others. Leadership experience can improve project delivery, retention, learning, and trust.\n\n### Long-term impact\nA leader's influence is multiplied through the capabilities they build in others. A person who hoards decisions may become a bottleneck; a person who teaches, delegates, and shares context creates more sustainable performance.\n\n### Case illustration\nA project coordinator initially solved every issue personally. As deadlines grew, work slowed. They introduced clear ownership, weekly coaching, and escalation rules. The team became more independent while the coordinator focused on risks and priorities.",
