  "summary": "A team lead aligns a project around customer needs, assigns owners, and reviews risks. A supervisor responds to a performance gap through clear feedback and support. A technical expert leads a safety ",
  "explanation": "### Workplace\nA team lead aligns a project around customer needs, assigns owners, and reviews risks. A supervisor responds to a performance gap through clear feedback and support. A technical expert leads a safety improvement without needing formal managerial authority.\n\n### Academic\nA student leader coordinates an event, distributes tasks fairly, and handles last-minute changes. A group-project leader ensures that every member understands expectations and receives credit.\n\n### Personal and community\nA volunteer coordinator schedules people, communicates changes, and resolves disagreements. A family member may demonstrate leadership by organizing a shared responsibility without controlling everyone.\n\n### Industry applications\nHealthcare leaders coordinate safe handovers; engineering leaders prioritize safety; technology leaders manage uncertainty; education leaders support learning; hospitality leaders maintain service quality under pressure.\n\n### Success pattern\nEffective leadership repeatedly follows a cycle: clarify purpose, understand people and constraints, decide responsibly, support execution, review results, and learn.",
