  "summary": "Lead by example. * Make purpose visible. * Listen before deciding. * Be consistent. * Give credit. * Admit mistakes. * Delegate outcomes, not just tasks. * Avoid public humiliation. * Explain trade-of",
  "explanation": "### Recommendations\nLead by example. * Make purpose visible. * Listen before deciding. * Be consistent. * Give credit. * Admit mistakes. * Delegate outcomes, not just tasks. * Avoid public humiliation. * Explain trade-offs. * Invite dissent. * Apply standards fairly. * Communicate changes early. * Protect capacity. * Coach instead of rescuing. * Separate facts from assumptions. * Review decisions. * Develop successors. * Keep promises. * Address misconduct. * Treat people with dignity.\n\n### Quick wins\nAsk your team what one obstacle you can remove, clarify one ambiguous responsibility, thank someone specifically, and explain the reason behind one decision.\n\n### Advanced mastery\nMastery includes balancing short-term execution with long-term capability, recognizing power dynamics, making ethical trade-offs, and building systems where leadership is shared rather than concentrated.",
