  "order": 3,
  "summary": "The Thinker's Toolkit -- Morgan D. Jones: practical analytical methods. Problem Solving 101 -- Ken Watanabe: accessible structured problem solving.\n\nThe Fifth Discipline -- Peter M. Senge: systems thi",
  "explanation": "### Books\nThe Thinker's Toolkit -- Morgan D. Jones: practical analytical methods. Problem Solving 101 -- Ken Watanabe: accessible structured problem solving.\n\nThe Fifth Discipline -- Peter M. Senge: systems thinking and learning organizations. Thinking, Fast and Slow -- Daniel Kahneman: judgment and cognitive biases.\n\nCreative Confidence -- Tom Kelley and David Kelley: creativity and experimentation. The Goal -- Eliyahu M. Goldratt: constraints and process thinking.\n\n### Online Courses\nCoursera: https://www.coursera.org/ -- courses in problem solving, critical thinking, design thinking, and decision making. edX: https://www.edx.org/ -- university-backed learning in critical thinking, systems, and innovation.\n\nMIT OpenCourseWare: https://ocw.mit.edu/ -- open course materials in engineering, management, and systems. Harvard Business School Online: https://online.hbs.edu/ -- professional resources on decision making and organizations.\n\n### Further Practice\nUniversity learning centers, quality-improvement communities, reputable management publications, case studies, and professional podcasts can provide additional practice. For daily practice, record the problem, evidence, options, decision, outcome, and lesson in a simple notes app or spreadsheet.",
