  "order": 2,
  "summary": "Rate each statement from 1 (rarely) to 5 (consistently): I clarify vague claims before judging them; I distinguish fact from inference; I look for relevant counterevidence; I compare multiple explanat",
  "explanation": "### Self-evaluation\nRate each statement from 1 (rarely) to 5 (consistently): I clarify vague claims before judging them; I distinguish fact from inference; I look for relevant counterevidence; I compare multiple explanations; I check source quality; I consider sample size and context; I identify assumptions; I communicate uncertainty; I can explain my reasoning simply; I revise a view when evidence changes; I use structured tools for complex decisions; I review past decisions for lessons; I invite respectful challenge.\n\nScoring guide: 52-65 indicates a strong routine, 39-51 indicates a developing routine, 26-38 indicates a useful improvement opportunity, and 13-25 suggests beginning with one habit at a time. The score is for reflection, not diagnosis. Read the individual items too: one very low item may matter more than a high total.\n\n### Reflection prompts\nWrite about a recent decision that did not go as expected. What assumption failed? What evidence did you overlook? Which alternative explanation should you have tested? Then write a \"next time\" rule in one sentence. Example: \"When a metric changes suddenly, I will check data quality and comparison periods before assigning a cause.\"",
