  "summary": "Rate 1 (rarely) to 5 (consistently): I define weekly outcomes; I distinguish urgent from important; I limit daily priorities; I break projects into clear next actions; I estimate realistically; I prot",
  "explanation": "### Self-evaluation\nRate 1 (rarely) to 5 (consistently): I define weekly outcomes; I distinguish urgent from important; I limit daily priorities; I break projects into clear next actions; I estimate realistically; I protect focused work; I control notifications; I use buffers; I communicate workload constraints; I review unfinished work; I delegate or automate appropriate tasks; I schedule recovery; I know where my time actually goes.\n\nScoring guide: 52-65 = strong system with opportunities to refine; 39-51 = developing system; 26-38 = inconsistent system needing a small number of foundational habits; 13-25 = start with capture, prioritization, and one daily focus block. Inspect individual scores because a single weak component, such as overcommitment, can undermine the rest.\n\n### Reflection prompts\nWhat important task was delayed this week, and why? Which interruption was avoidable? Where did your estimate differ from reality? What commitment should have been renegotiated sooner? Which habit created the most useful improvement? Write one rule for next week, such as \"I will not accept a new deadline until I check my current capacity.\"",
