  "summary": "Books:\n\nCracking the Coding Interview by Gayle Laakmann McDowell - technical interview preparation for software candidates.\n\nThe 2-Hour Job Search by Steve Dalton - practical networking and job-search",
  "explanation": "### Summary\nBooks:\n\nCracking the Coding Interview by Gayle Laakmann McDowell - technical interview preparation for software candidates.\n\nThe 2-Hour Job Search by Steve Dalton - practical networking and job-search methods.\n\nWhat Color Is Your Parachute? by Richard N. Bolles - career exploration and job-search strategy.\n\nKnock 'em Dead by Martin Yate - career and interview preparation guidance.\n\nThe Interview Book by James Innes - broad interview preparation and question practice.\n\nDesigning Your Life by Bill Burnett and Dave Evans - structured career exploration and experimentation.\n\nOnline resources:\n\nCoursera - search for interview preparation, career success, behavioral interviewing, and technical interview courses.\n\nLinkedIn Learning - interview preparation, job search, communication, and career development courses.\n\nedX - career and professional communication courses.\n\nBig Interview - interview practice and feedback resources.\n\nToastmasters International - practice for concise professional speaking and confidence.\n\nUseful tools include spreadsheets for competency mapping, calendars for preparation milestones, recording apps for mock interviews, and note systems for tracking questions and lessons. For technical roles, use\n\nrole-specific practice environments and official documentation for the technologies named in the job description.\n\nAlways verify current course availability and hiring-process details from the employer's official recruitment information. Interview formats vary by organization and role.",
